# Worker comments and OpenSpec task IDs

When developing an OpenSpec task, read the applicable change's task identifiers in `tasks.md` and linked spec or plan documents before editing. Do not put any of those identifiers in a new or substantively revised comment in first-party source, tests, scripts, or configuration files, including GoDoc and Rust doc comments. This covers dotted IDs such as `2.1` and letter-number IDs such as `F-01` when they identify tasks. Describe the feature, contract, or boundary instead.

Before handing off the work, inspect added and revised comments for those identifiers. Task IDs may be used in the task brief, OpenSpec artifacts, and ledger entries; they do not belong in implementation comments. Follow the project-wide rule in `AGENTS.md`.
